                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "832bd023-b6e6-4b88-9d87-fb5b00a399bf",
                                "sense_id": "691f509d-e989-3ea8-a584-0459a320b0eb",
                                "text": "In a project involving many people, maintainability is a more useful asset than perfectibility."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fdd3b610-76e2-47c7-8a03-ca26a055b74f",
                                "sense_id": "691f509d-e989-3ea8-a584-0459a320b0eb",
                                "text": "Thus it was that I beheld, as never before, the awful unreality called evil. The equipollence of God brought to light another glorious proposition, — man’s perfectibility and the establishment of the kingdom of heaven on earth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91de600f-a8b5-4bcf-b1e8-21990f946bcf",
                                "sense_id": "691f509d-e989-3ea8-a584-0459a320b0eb",
                                "text": "In their evangelical zeal, crusaders relied upon a message of the essential morality of cleanliness, a message that was especially effective in stirring religious sentiment and that meshed well with evolutionary models of human perfectibility that were prevalent in the sciences."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
